# 7. BLE Signaling Server

Implement:

BleSignalingServer.kt

The Android device acts as a BLE Peripheral / GATT Server.

The iPhone will later act as the BLE Central using CoreBluetooth.

Use a stable custom service UUID.

Create two characteristics.

## Characteristic 1: CALL_STATE_CHAR

Properties:

- READ
- NOTIFY

Purpose:

Send cellular call information and device status to the iPhone.

Example JSON:

{
  "version": 1,
  "type": "CALL_STATE",
  "state": "RINGING",
  "callId": "call_123",
  "number": "+98912XXXXXXXX",
  "displayName": null,
  "endpoint": {
    "host": "192.168.43.1",
    "port": 8080
  },
  "audioCapability": "CELLULAR_AUDIO_UNAVAILABLE",
  "timestamp": 1790000000
}

Do not hardcode the example IP address.

Resolve the actual active network address dynamically.

## Characteristic 2: COMMAND_CHAR

Properties:

- WRITE
- WRITE_WITHOUT_RESPONSE where appropriate

Accept commands from the iPhone.

Example commands:

Answer incoming call:

{
  "version": 1,
  "id": "cmd_001",
  "cmd": "ACCEPT"
}

Reject incoming call:

{
  "version": 1,
  "id": "cmd_002",
  "cmd": "REJECT"
}

End active call:

{
  "version": 1,
  "id": "cmd_003",
  "cmd": "HANGUP"
}

Initiate outgoing call:

{
  "version": 1,
  "id": "cmd_004",
  "cmd": "DIAL",
  "number": "+98912XXXXXXXX"
}

The server must validate every incoming command.

Use a response protocol with matching command IDs.

Example:

{
  "version": 1,
  "type": "COMMAND_RESULT",
  "id": "cmd_001",
  "success": true,
  "message": "Call answered"
}

